 That install applies to "Flink CD32" © 1994 Psygnosis.

 That install requires WHDLoad version 16.0 to be in the path. It can be found
 in the WHDLoad package.

 You need 2.0 MB ChipMem and 0.5 MB OtherMem.
 You can quit the game by pressing '*' on the numeric keypad (key can be
 changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A600/A1200/A4000 Kickstart 3.1 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick40063.A600", "kick40068.A1200" or "kick40068.A4000". The
 image can be extracted from an A600/A1200/A4000 with tools like 'GrabKick' or
 similar which can be found on Aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick40063.A600.RTB", "kick40068.A1200.RTB" or
 "kick40068.A4000.RTB" must be installed in the same directory as the kickstart
 image. It can be found in the archive "util/boot/skick346.lha" on Aminet.

 The game is designed for joypad use only. To make it playable with a joystick
 too a joypad emulation via the keyboard has been implemented. The default
 joypad to keyboard assignment is as follows:
	Blue - Stop		- F1 (Action)
	Green - Shuffle		- F2 (NTSC/PAL)
	Yellow - Repeat		- F3 (Cast spell)
	Grey - Play/Pause	- F4 (Pause)
 You can change the keys using the Custom tooltype. The template for the string
 is "Blue/K,Green/K,Yellow/K,Grey/K,LeftEar/K,RightEar/K,Force/S".
 Example to set Grey button to Space and Blue to Del:
	Custom=grey $40 blue $46
 To make lowlevel.library detect a joystick you must move the stick right/left
 or up/down a few times. After this the emulation will start to work.
 You can also add/use the option Force to the Custom tooltype to disable the
 auto sensing of the lowlevel.library and to force it to assume a joystick is
 connected and enable the joypad emulation.
	Custom=grey $40 blue $46 force

 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

 Features:
 - joypad is emulated by joystick + keyboard (F1-F4)
 - nice NI/MWB icons included
 - source: https://github.com/wepl/winstalls/tree/master/games/Flink

 Note:
 - Since there is an extra life at the first level no trainer is needed, you
   can get an unlimited amount of lives by getting it, leaving the level and
   playing it again

 Thanks to:
 - Don Adan for the original files from CD32 version.

 History:
 - V1.3, July 2000: sound and crash in certain spells fixed by Harry

 Mr.Larmer/Wanted Team in 1999 and Harry in July 2000.

 version 2.0 (07.07.04) by Wepl:
 - reworked for kickemu
 - to save disk space and memory for preload you may uncompress (XFD) and
   afterwards compress (ProPack) all *.wld and *.raw files

 version 2.1 (31.08.05) by Wepl:
 - joypad emulation has now user definable keys
 - works with caches on 68060 (blitter interrupt handling fixed)
 - correct language is automatically set

 version 2.2 (14.12.05) by CFOU!/Wepl:
 - problems with nonworking blue button when using joypad fixed
 - sound problems fixed (more chip memory required)
 - some color icons added

 version 2.3 (30.05.09) by Wepl:
 - language detection fixed (Italian was defaulted to Spanish), thanks to
   Hexaae for the report

 version 2.4 (09.06.09) by Wepl:
 - joypad emulation now supports the Force keyword to disable auto sensing and
   force joystick mode
